</ul>

<h2 id="quality">4. Data quality</h2>
<div class="question">What is wrong with the raw data, how big is each problem, and what did we do about it?</div>
<div class="fig" id="fig-issues">{{ figs.issues | safe }}</div>
<div class="scroll">{{ tables.issues | safe }}</div>
<div class="grid2">
  <div class="fig">{{ figs.coverage | safe }}</div>
  <div class="fig">{{ figs.lifecycle | safe }}</div>
</div>
<div class="fig">{{ figs.nulls | safe }}</div>
<div class="fig">{{ figs.payments | safe }}</div>
<p>Payments should equal items plus freight. At a R$1 tolerance, {{ n.mismatch|int }} of {{ n.mismatch_base|int }} orders differ; {{ n.mismatch_installments|int }} of them are card payments in installments, which points to installment interest. GMV (items + freight) is therefore the revenue measure, and payments are kept as a separate measure (ADR 0004).</p>

<h2 id="tests">5. Tests and CI</h2>
